(TIM-05 - the seven time properties are read with the `'s` possessive and
 each lands inside the range the manual's table gives it. Clock-dependent
 values are checked rather than printed, so this probe's output is the
 same on every run (the rule 'gen leaf timer and clock' already follows).
 Also covers: TIM-04, TIM-06, TIM-07, TIM-08, TIM-09, TIM-10, TIM-11.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox TIM-05.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   hour is 0 to 23
   minute is 0 to 59
   second is 0 to 59
   day is 1 to 31
   month is 1 to 12
   year is at least 2026
   unix is seconds since the epoch
)
Get current time into now.
If now's hour is greater than or equal to 0 and now's hour is less than 24 then, print "hour is 0 to 23".
Otherwise, print "hour is out of range: {now's hour}".
If now's minute is greater than or equal to 0 and now's minute is less than 60 then, print "minute is 0 to 59".
Otherwise, print "minute is out of range: {now's minute}".
If now's second is greater than or equal to 0 and now's second is less than 60 then, print "second is 0 to 59".
Otherwise, print "second is out of range: {now's second}".
If now's day is greater than 0 and now's day is less than 32 then, print "day is 1 to 31".
Otherwise, print "day is out of range: {now's day}".
If now's month is greater than 0 and now's month is less than 13 then, print "month is 1 to 12".
Otherwise, print "month is out of range: {now's month}".
If now's year is greater than 2025 then, print "year is at least 2026".
Otherwise, print "year is out of range: {now's year}".
If now's unix is greater than 1750000000 then, print "unix is seconds since the epoch".
Otherwise, print "unix is too small to be an epoch second count: {now's unix}".
